        "user": "You are synthesizing this {{period_label}}'s {{topic_focus}} research with deep analysis of top papers.\n\n## STATISTICS OVERVIEW\n```json\n{{stats_json}}\n\n## ANALYZED PAPERS with full-text analysis)\n```json\n{{analyzed_papers_json}}\n```\n## ADDITIONAL RELEVANT PAPERS ({{remaining_count}} papers - no full-text analysis)\n\n## PRIORITIZED REMAINING PAPERS CONTEXT (capped)\nSelection policy used upstream: {{remaining_selection_policy}}\n```json\n{{remaining_papers_json}}\n```\n\n\n## YOUR TASK\n\nWrite a professional {{period_label}} research digest email with this structure:\n\n### Email Body Structure:\n\n**Opening**: \"Hey there, Here's your {{period_label}} roundup of {{topic_focus}} research from arXiv.\n\n**## Executive Summary**\n\n\nExecutive-summary linking requirements:\n- Include exactly one top-paper recommendation sentence in Executive Summary as a Markdown hyperlink in this exact format: [Paper Title](arxiv_id).\n- The hyperlink URL must exactly match the selected paper's arxiv_id from ANALYZED PAPERS JSON (no fabricated or random links).\n- The linked paper must be the same paper you name as the top recommendation.\n\nWrite 3-4 sentences highlighting the most significant developments during {{period_label}}. What are the key themes? \nWhat is the one paper from the most influential research lab/company/university about memory architecture (HBM or other high-performance memory) in the context of AI that you would recommend and why?\n\n**## Deep Dive: Top Research**\n\nGroup the analyzed papers by research theme if such themese are present.\n\nFor each theme:\n- Write 2-4 sentences of context\n- Write a thematic introduction (3-5 sentences) explaining why this area is active and what trends you observe\n- Use the short_summary verbatim for each paper (DO NOT modify or paraphrase)\n- NEVER use LaTeX, MathJax, or dollar-sign math notation. Write equations in plain text.\n- Start each paper with a title+affiliation line as its own line (hyperlinked): [Name or title of paper or affiliation if important](arxiv_id)\n- Then insert a blank line and place the short_summary on the next line\n- If pdf_analysis_performed is false for a paper, note: \"(Note: Full-text analysis unavailable)\" on its own line after the short_summary\n\n**## Media Intelligence**\n\nAdd this section after \"Deep Dive: Top Research\" only when such sources are available in the provided MEDIA INTELLIGENCE data.\nDo not fabricate announcements, blog posts, analyst takes, or expert commentary.\n\nDo NOT include a separate section titled \"Additional Relevant Papers\".\nIf there are remaining papers, summarize them only through the \"Also Worth Noting\" section using the provided prioritized context.\n\n**## Also Worth Noting**\n\nList 5-10 papers from the prioritized remaining context, prioritizing analyzed-but-not-selected papers when available.\n\nFormatting and content rules:\n- Do NOT use bullets, numbered lists, or list markers for this section.\n- Write each entry as a standalone short paragraph in the same visual style as other paper cards.\n- Each entry must be exactly one sentence.\n- Use this format: [Paper Title](arxiv_id) — Institution(s): one objective, evidence-grounded reason it is interesting.\n- Use ONLY papers present in the PRIORITIZED REMAINING PAPERS CONTEXT JSON above. Prioritize entries sourced from analyzed-but-not-selected papers before non-analyzed fallback entries.\n- Prioritize first papers where relevance_score or credibility_tier is 10, then by relevance_score + credibility_tier.\n- Do not invent papers, links, institutions, or scores not present in the provided context.\n- Keep statements strictly factual and verifiable from the provided data; avoid projections, speculation, or forward-looking claims.\n\nWhen rendering **This Last Week in Numbers**:\n- Use the provided {{this_period_numbers}} content exactly as the source of truth.\n- Do not paraphrase or rewrite the numeric lines; preserve metric labels and values so downstream formatting can parse them reliably.\n- Keep these phrases intact when present: \"paper abstracts analyzed\", \"deemed relevant\", \"papers received full-text deep analysis\", \"Top research themes\", \"Quality metrics\", \"high-credibility institutions\".\n\n**## This Last Week in Numbers**\nUse this data coming in from the analysis:\n{{this_period_numbers}}\n\n**Closing**: \"Until next time,\n\n{{assistant_signature}}\"\n\n## OUTPUT FORMAT\n\nReturn pure JSON (no code fences):\n{\n\"subject\": \"MIRA {{mode_label}} Digest - Top {{topic_short_label}} Papers Published on Arxiv and Notable News Articles - {{current_date}} - [X scanned, Y analyzed]\",\n\"body\": \"[Full email in Markdown format]\"\n}\n\nCRITICAL: \n- Use short_summary text EXACTLY as provided - do not rephrase or modify.\n- Prioritize industry insights over purely research insights in the way you order your report.",
